WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:04.560
The Networking exam tests your foundational&nbsp;
knowledge of networking concepts and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.520
administration. It is a conceptual exam, meaning&nbsp;
that you do not need to possess the knowledge of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:13.600
a full-fledged network administrator. Still,&nbsp;
you need to know basic networking concepts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:17.680
and how they fit into the grand scheme&nbsp;
of building and maintaining a network.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.240
To that point, we will take you through&nbsp;
this course as if you work for TekkieVets,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:27.680
an IT consulting company, and you are a candidate&nbsp;
to be promoted from a help desk support agent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.720
to a junior-level network administrator. To that&nbsp;
end, we will cover the basics of network building&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:38.480
and administration among these five exam domains:&nbsp;
Networking Fundamentals, Network Infrastructure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:45.200
Network Hardware, Protocols and Services, and&nbsp;
Troubleshooting. Make sure you pay close attention&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.280
to the whats, as in what are these different&nbsp;
parts of a network? To follow along with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.360
live demos in this course, you will want to have a&nbsp;
couple of Windows devices connected to each other,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.600
or at least one Windows device,&nbsp;
an installation of Windows server,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:02.160
and if you can get your hands on a wireless access&nbsp;
point to configure, all the better. Getting some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.720
hands-on practice will solidify your knowledge&nbsp;
of the concepts we are covering in this course.

